{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1\\cdot (-9)-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+(-9)+20=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be1228233b5c5998d375573ded6049a6d32da6f1eafbc232ed875502a951058"} {"question" "q-124224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-13"] ["math" "-33"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -3 \\\\ 1 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be1228233b5c5998d375573ded6049a6d32da6f1eafbc232ed875502a951058"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v+1,\\,y=9u-4v+3.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+a,\\,v=by+cx+3,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v+1 \\\\ 9u-4v+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 9u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ y-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-3) \\\\ -9\\cdot (x-1)+2\\cdot (y-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y-4x+1 \\\\ 2y-9x+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+1,\\,v=2y+(-9)x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+(-9)=-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be1228233b5c5998d375573ded6049a6d32da6f1eafbc232ed875502a951058"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-12"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=-2v-4,\\,y=u+4v+6.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=2x+y+a,\\,v=bx+cy-2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v-4 \\\\ u+4v+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v \\\\ u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+4 \\\\ y-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (x+4)+1\\cdot (y-6) \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (x+4)+0\\cdot (y-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}x-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x+y+2,\\,v=(-\\frac{1}{2})x+0y-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+(-\\frac{1}{2})+0=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be1228233b5c5998d375573ded6049a6d32da6f1eafbc232ed875502a951058"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-124316" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/assets/c1ee8bc2c212708ed583c709420a856b28f6e2129c24690a504b4716b2692aa7.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=u-2v+1,\\,y=2u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v+1 \\\\ 2u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible and the image of the triangle under the action of $T$ is a triangle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be1228233b5c5998d375573ded6049a6d32da6f1eafbc232ed875502a951058"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A line segment"] ["text" "A parallelogram"] ["text" "A point"] ["text" "A square"] ["text" "A triangle"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"} {"question" "q-162217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A triangle"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9d2606d472ed9e3b2e93659cb2939223edf6e5523451520a3263d753eacc858"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1685 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
